 "rules_history": [
  {
   "change": "first lock, copied from SPEC.md and FLAGSHIP.md",
   "date": "2026-09-30",
   "version": 1
  },
  {
   "change": "Cam chose option A for the flagship (D3 with D2): CES SM for 2019->2025 across the 150 largest metros by CES total nonfarm 2019; twins pooled under the Jul 2023 composition, failing closed for metros with no 2019 vector; H3 prints each axis's rank; the QCEW native MSA rows for 2019->2023 become registered row X1. Decided before any twin result was computed (docs/DECISIONS.md).",
   "date": "2026-10-01",
   "version": 2
  },
  {
   "change": "The orchestrating agent fixed mtnn.epochs = 200 for R3 and R4 (same objective and sampler): the last epoch is kept, with no early stopping and no checkpoint chosen on any scored split; the count comes from compute and the vector-realty recipe, never from a val score. S0.5(b) stays as registered (option (a)): the MTNN is still trained and reported in M8, but gates_passed (SPEC 6.3 step 5(d)) reads reports/stage0_model.json S0.5b.pass = false, so it can't be kept in v0 and the release ships on B*. Decided before any R3 or R4 had been trained to a registered epoch count and before any trained-model PS existed on val; the MDE lock is regenerated under rules_version 3 with M5's MDE and eval-set hash. Cam can overrule (docs/DECISIONS.md).",
   "date": "2026-10-01",
   "version": 3
